        {
          "provider": "Flickr",
          "id": "9295522546",
          "title": "Not a mysterious misty scene this!",
          "description": "The following day was the day of our departure for Manila. But before that, we had another programme on the itinerary. This is the dolphin watching tour, which meant a bloody early start of 05:45. So here we aer, on the banca (traditional Filipino boat) casting off for the dolphins tour. And no, this is not a mysterious and romantic scene in the mist and gof. It was bloody hot and humid at 05:45 in the morning, and my lens has fogged completely. Wiping it clean meant it getting fogged again. Now the banquero (boat man) will not wait indefinitely for my lens to be clean, so he cast off anyway, after waiting some 10min. So this is a crisp, early morning though humid scene shot with a completely fogged lens. (Bohol- Tagbilaran, Philippines, May 2013)",
          "creator": "shankar s.",
          "owner": "77742560@N06",
          "sourcePage": "https://www.flickr.com/photos/shankaronline/9295522546/",
          "licenseCode": 4,
          "originalUrl": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7405/9295522546_550df65366_b.jpg",
